  "description": "This course provides a foundational understanding of computer vision, focusing on Python-based image processing and analysis techniques. Students will explore the representation and manipulation of visual data, covering image structures, raster and vector formats, and essential operations: filtering, and transformations. Advanced topics include feature detection, matching, and introductory object detection. By the end of the course, students will be equipped to implement core computer vision techniques and analyze visual data, laying the groundwork for more complex applications in the field.",
